<title>USA: Farmington, N.M., pollution control $65 mln priced.</title>
<headline>Farmington, N.M., pollution control $65 mln priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Tuesday it tentatively priced $65 million of Farmington, N.M., pollution control revenue refunding bonds, 1996 Series C, with a top yield of 5.70 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds are AMBAC insured.</p>
<p>City of Farmington, New Mexico</p>
<p>RE: $65,000,000*</p>
<p>Pollution Control Revenue</p>
<p>Refunding Bonds, 1996 Series C</p>
<p>(Public Service Company of New Mexico San Juan Project)</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 12/05/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>12/01/2016	     65,000M    5.70  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 12/01/2006 at 102.00, DTP 12/01/2008</p>
<p>The award is expected Tuesday, November 19, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on December 5, 1996.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>Citicorp Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>BA Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Rauscher Pierce Refsnes, Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
